── THE ELECTRIC FIELD (2026-10-01): dark purple electricity crawling over the black gate and radiating off it ──────────
   · BOLTS — jagged arcs between points on the frame and out into the air, re-struck every ~70 ms (one LineSegments, one draw);
   · WAVES — rings pulsing outward from the mouth and across the floor, fading as they spread (5 meshes);
   · SPARKS — shed from the bolts with real motion: velocity, gravity, drag, a bounce off the floor, a fade (one Points draw).
   No light is created (a new light recompiles every lit material in r128). Animated only while the player is near.
   Off: window._toriiElectric = false.

── THE GHOSTS IN LINE, THE WAY A KID PICTURES THEM (Mark 2026-09-26: "fix it so it looks cooler, the way kids would imagine?").
   The three hungry-ghost patrons (the memorial queue — "waiting forever for the shop that never closes") now:
     · FLOAT — each hovers _ghostHover (0.28) above the floor on its own slow bob and sway, a soft glow pooled beneath it
       (one additive plane each, no light — FPS law), all facing the door;
     · ARE GHOSTS — players and monsters pass straight through them (the peer and shove tests skip storeGhost bodies), so the line
       never clogs the passage it stands in;
     · CHAT — every 14-24 s, while the player is within 8 tiles and the shop is shut, one says something kid-sized in a bubble;
     · GO IN WHEN IT OPENS — the moment the shop opens (the Tenchō won, or a STORE permit), they cheer, then drift to the door one by
       one and vanish inside in a gold sparkle: after all that waiting, they finally get their snacks.
   Off: window._konbiniGhostLife = false (the old pinned standing line).

── ANTS ARE PESTS (Mark 2026-09-26) — what an ant counts as food, and what happens when it eats. GOHAN and RICE BALL anywhere;
   in the cafeteria and the storage room EVERY card is supplies. Each card eaten lays an egg (below), which hatches while fewer
   than _antHatchCap (20) ants live — Mark: "cap at 20 live at any one time". Doors are the real limit: ants cannot open them.

TO THE DOOR, THEN LEAN, THEN TALK (2026-10-19, Mark: "if jester is speaking, he must go to nearest door between player and jester and then
   lean over to chat"): while a line waits he runs to the door tile that can see the player with the shortest jester→door→player trip;
   standing on it he leans (st.talkPeek feeds the tilt law) and the peek gate above lets the line out. Off: window._jesterTalkDoor = false.

UNWEDGE (SEEN 2026-10-19, Playwright, three boots): a shoo flip carries him 1 wu along an arbitrary yaw, so he can stop off-grid inside a thin wall's buffer;
   from there _canMonsterStand refuses the first sample of every route step and the escape repaths forever (9.5 wu from the portal for 45 s, no neighbour,
   no one-shot). After a flip, and whenever an escape step stays blocked, he is set on the nearest standable floor tile centre within one tile.
   knowledge/design/JESTER_VENT_RULES_2026-10-19.md

THE GUARDS' ROUTINE (2026-10-03, CLAUDE.md GAME FACT): once a second, every guard (_isGuard) —
  PROTECT  a worker struck within 8 tiles in the last 3 s turns it on the attacker (its job);
  ASIDE    the player within 1.5 tiles: it steps 2 tiles out of the way;
  BOW      the player in sight within 5 tiles: it faces the player and bows, once per meeting (the real bow only when its rig has
           a bow clip — a forced bow on a rig without one plays the wrong clip — else it faces the player with a 🙇 bubble);
  WATCH    otherwise, standing idle within 8 tiles, it turns to face the player;
  WANDER   idle and not watching: it walks to a random reachable tile within 8, every 6-14 s.
Hostile, charging, asleep, an ally or dead: left alone. Knob: window._guardBrain = false (off).

