── Ranged KITER — LEASHED + CATCHABLE (Mark 2026-06-25) ──
The imp is a missile monster: it keeps its distance and drifts toward cover after
firing, but it MUST stay catchable. Three guarantees against the 2026-06-24
kite-forever lockup: (1) LEASH — never retreat more than _impKiteLeash tiles from
where it stood when the player breached kite range, so it can't run down a corridor;
(2) SLOW — back-pedal slower than the player chases, so the player always closes;
(3) HOLD — if every retreat tile is blocked it slides toward a doorway/corner, and
if fully boxed in it simply holds and keeps firing (hittable). NO never-melee gate,
NO long pathfind — those caused the lockup. All three are knob-tunable in-chat.

Face direction of travel — but HOLD facing while WEDGED (ud._fleeStuck, set last frame when no move
succeeded) to kill the in-place spin/shake (Mark 2026-06-23). Mirrors the chase facing gate on _stuckSince;
resumes turning the instant a real (or corner-slide) move lands. Door transit keeps moving → never stuck.

